Your executable contains instruction(s) which cannot be directly executed by
your hardware; eg. a byte/word load/store needs a processor of type EV56 or
greater. If you run it on EV5 or less the OS will emulate the instruction.

Look at the 'iec' command and the '-arch' option of the 'cc' compiler. I
can't comment on 'gcc'.

Eckhardt





